 "prompt": "The repository at /testbed has a bug, described below. Fix it by changing the source code; do not modify or\nadd tests. When you are done, the project's existing test suite should pass.\n\n<issue>\n# Conditional INSERT statements with WHEN/THEN/ELSE fail to parse correctly\n\n## Description\n\nI've encountered an issue with parsing conditional INSERT statements in Oracle dialect. The parser fails to correctly handle the WHEN/THEN/ELSE syntax in multi-table inserts.\n\n## Code to Reproduce\n\n```sql\n-- This fails to parse correctly\nINSERT FIRST \nWHEN id <= 3 THEN \n  INTO dest_tab1 (id, description) VALUES (id, description) \nWHEN id <= 5 THEN \n  INTO dest_tab2 (id, description) VALUES (id, description) \nELSE \n  INTO dest_tab3 (id, description) VALUES (id, description) \nSELECT id, description FROM source_tab\n```\n\n```python\nfrom sqlglot import parse_one\n\n# This will fail\nsql = \"\"\"\nINSERT FIRST \nWHEN id <= 3 THEN \n  INTO dest_tab1 (id, description) VALUES (id, description) \nWHEN id <= 5 THEN \n  INTO dest_tab2 (id, description) VALUES (id, description) \nELSE \n  INTO dest_tab3 (id, description) VALUES (id, description) \nSELECT id, description FROM source_tab\n\"\"\"\n\nparsed = parse_one(sql)  # This raises an error\n```\n\n## Problem Details\n\nThe issue appears to be in the `parse_conditional_insert` method in the parser. When trying to parse Oracle's conditional multi-table INSERT statements, the parser fails to correctly handle the WHEN/THEN/ELSE syntax structure.\n\nThe problem specifically occurs with:\n1. The condition parsing after WHEN\n2. The handling of the ELSE clause\n3. The structure of nested INSERT statements within the conditional blocks\n\n## Expected Behavior\n\nThe parser should correctly handle Oracle's conditional INSERT syntax, including:\n- INSERT ALL / INSERT FIRST statements\n- WHEN conditions followed by THEN\n- Multiple WHEN/THEN blocks\n- ELSE clauses\n- Proper nesting of the INSERT statements within these conditional blocks\n\nThis is a critical feature for anyone working with Oracle databases that use conditional multi-table inserts.\n</issue>\n",
